Execution Control Commands
--start-at-task="TASK NAME"  
Resume playbook from a specific task.

--step  
Run playbook interactively, asking before each task.

--tags / --skip-tags  
Run only tasks with certain tags or skip them.

bash
ansible-playbook site.yml --tags "deploy"
ansible-playbook site.yml --skip-tags "cleanup"
--limit  
Restrict execution to specific hosts.

bash
ansible-playbook site.yml --limit web01
--check  
Dry-run mode (no changes applied, just shows what would happen).

--diff  
Show differences when files/templates change.



Debugging & Verbosity
-v, -vv, -vvv  
Increase verbosity for debugging.

bash
ansible-playbook site.yml -vvv
--list-hosts  
Show which hosts will be affected.

Show all tasks in the playbook.

--list-tags  
Show available tags.

⚡ Performance & Parallelism
-f <N>  
Forks: run tasks in parallel across N hosts.

bash
ansible-playbook site.yml -f 20
serial (inside playbook)  
Run hosts in batches.

yaml
- hosts: webservers
  serial: 2


Error Handling
--force-handlers  
Run handlers even if a task fails.

--skip-tags  
Skip problematic tasks temporarily.

ignore_errors: yes (inside playbook)
Continue even if a task fails.


##############
# Resume from a failed task
ansible-playbook deploy.yml --start-at-task="Configure DB"

# Dry run with diff
ansible-playbook site.yml --check --diff

# Run only on failed hosts
ansible-playbook site.yml --limit failed_hosts

# Run only tasks tagged 'deploy'
ansible-playbook site.yml --tags deploy
